# Fixture for native_codegen.feature: docs/plans/general-refcounting.md
# Phase 2's own extension to main/handler functions, not just ordinary
# callee functions. main itself only ever runs once per process, so
# unlike the callee-function fixtures in this same directory, there's
# no later allocation WITHIN the same run that could show the freed
# block being reused -- the meaningful proof here is correctness (no
# crash, no corrupted output), not a heap-growth measurement, since the
# underlying rt_string_rc_dec mechanism is already exhaustively proven
# by this plan's earlier increments. Verified against pat --ir-run on
# the identical source, this suite's own established cross-check.

let s1 = chr(65)
print(s1)
let s2 = chr(66)
print(s2)
let s3 = chr(67)
print(s3)
